1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:09,730
A loan file rarely fakes a whole document. It changes one number. Here the payslip says 86,500, but its own arithmetic and its own words say 68,500.

2
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:20,230
SAKSHI runs the ten stages from the brief. Each finding is weighed by how reliable its witness is, must survive its innocent explanations, and lands on one of three rungs. It never says fraud.

3
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:26,030
A tampered loan application: five documents, nine planted manipulations. Memory is cleared first, so nothing is remembered from earlier runs.

4
00:00:26,030 --> 00:00:29,496
Ten stages run on this laptop: documents are read one by one, then judged together.

5
00:00:29,496 --> 00:00:34,616
Potential manipulation, inconsistencies, observations. The processing time is the real, unedited run time.

6
00:00:36,566 --> 00:00:43,626
As submitted: 86,500. The smallest change that makes every rule hold: 68,500, the real salary, recovered.

7
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:48,376
Nine pixel sensors plus the PDF’s own structure. A pasted or whited-out region shows up in the noise map.

8
00:00:48,376 --> 00:00:52,646
Each field is marked strong, weak or blind, so the analyst knows what still needs a human check.

9
00:00:52,646 --> 00:00:55,816
Every step is logged with the hash of the step before it, so a later edit to the record is detectable.

10
00:00:55,826 --> 00:00:59,786
The same applicant’s genuine documents. A useful forensic tool stays quiet on honest paperwork.

11
00:00:59,786 --> 00:01:03,013
Same ten stages, same thresholds.

12
00:01:03,013 --> 00:01:08,153
No potential manipulation and no inconsistency. One observation, explained.

13
00:01:08,253 --> 00:01:15,663
Case three is a red-team attack: a scanned payslip edited in a PDF editor. The scan is untouched; a box hides the real figure and new text sits on top.

14
00:01:15,663 --> 00:01:20,233
Red-team case RT8, loaded from the console’s demo list.

15
00:01:20,233 --> 00:01:23,381
The console runs each case in its own worker process, so a stalled case is stopped instead of freezing it.

16
00:01:23,381 --> 00:01:27,921
Five potential-manipulation findings.

17
00:01:29,701 --> 00:01:35,701
What a reader sees: 88,500. The scan inside the same file, underneath: 68,500.

18
00:01:35,751 --> 00:01:46,371
Every number comes from a test anyone can rerun, including where SAKSHI fails: on real receipts the middle tier cannot separate forged from genuine.

19
00:01:46,371 --> 00:01:52,071
SAKSHI. Evidence, not verdicts.
